A panel hierarchy is meaningless for a single panel detector, and is now banned for one. Previously the geometry of such a detector could be split between its root node and its panel, with ``set_fast_slow_beam_centre_mm`` and ``set_detector_distance`` moving the root while DIALS refinement moved the panel, so that the two drifted apart. These helpers now move the panel, a ``Format`` class that builds a single panel detector with a hierarchy raises, and an experiment list written by an earlier version has the root node folded into its panel on read, leaving the panel in exactly the same place.
